            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Famistar sells them under its own name from its web store and on Walmart.com, but it does not name a manufacturer or parent company, and we could not confirm one. The store also sells mattresses, luggage, air fryers and pet products, which is typical of a marketplace home-goods brand that sources from contract manufacturers.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Are Famistar treadmills good?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "They can be reasonable for light walking at a low price, but we found no independent review of a current model, and the listings contradict themselves on motors, weight limits and warranty length. Buy at the low end of the range, plan around the lowest figure on any listing, and get the warranty and return terms in writing.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the weight limit on the Famistar T532?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The listing gives a range, 300 to 400 lb, and says 300 lb reflects conservative standards while 400 lb is the tested figure. A weight limit should be a single conservative number, so plan around 300 lb and leave a margin below that, especially since the motor is described only by its peak rating.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What warranty comes with a Famistar treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Famistar’s own website gives three answers: 365 days on the home page, 12 months in the refund policy, and a free 6-month warranty on the contact page. We cannot say which the company would honour. Ask for the length and coverage in writing before ordering, including who pays shipping on a warranty claim.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can I return a Famistar treadmill if I change my mind?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Under the store’s refund policy, free returns within 30 days are for approved reasons such as defects or shipping damage. For a change of mind, an order made by mistake or a machine that does not meet expectations, the buyer pays return shipping and restocking. Walmart purchases follow the return terms shown on that listing.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is the Famistar W500C still sold?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No. An independent repair and review site noted years ago that the W500C had left Famistar’s website, and it is not on the current store. It was an entry-level folding treadmill with a 1.5 HP motor, a 15.7 by 43.3-inch running area, a top speed of about 6 mph and a 240 lb limit.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-10-14",
      dateModified: "2026-10-14",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
  ],
